  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Recorded on Sunday, June 15, 2014, at Bottom of the Hill in San Francisco, this performance captures the Mountain Goats in a complete twenty-five song set [1][3]. The recommended recording is a matrix mix that blends soundboard audio with audience microphones, providing a balanced view of the live event [1]. Taped by an anonymous contributor and transferred by BLG, the file offers a documented lineage and lossless quality [1]. The setlist features several tracks that are exceptionally rare in the archive’s history [3]. For example, Move (Chicago 196?) is the only archived performance of that song, while Ice Cream, Cobra Man has only three archived performances [3]. This Magic Moment is also mythic rare, with just two archived performances [3]. Other bustout songs include Running Away With What Freud Said and Going To Alaska [3]. The show concludes with a long encore that includes Going to Maine and Jenny [3]. This is the second consecutive night the band played at this venue, following a show on June 14, 2014 [3]. As the 198th show in the archive’s collection for the band, it represents a significant entry in their discography [3]. An alternative audience recording from the same date is also available, but the matrix mix is preferred for its technical qualities [1][2]. The total runtime is approximately 94 minutes, covering the full duration of the show [1][3].",
